<title>SOUTH AFRICA: PRESMED HALF YR SHR RISES, NO DIV.</title>
<headline>PRESMED HALF YR SHR RISES, NO DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     </p>
<p>    - undiluted	     24.7	    vs 20.6</p>
<p>    - diluted		 23.0	    vs 18.9</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   13.47	   vs 8.62</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   18.28	   vs 10.72</p>
<p>    Tax			 4.40	    vs 2.11</p>
<p>    Interest		  0.90 received vs 0.30 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  166.39	  vs 102.43</p>
<p>Full name: President Medical Investments Ltd </p>
<p>NOTE - Directors expect satisfactory earnings growth in the</p>
<p>current financial year. They said the merger with Lifecare</p>
<p>Clinics had potential for the group in the medium- to long term.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings figures have been restated to</p>
<p>take into account a 1:10 capitalisation issue in July 1996.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
